{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the J4 implementation boundary (request 0c3091fa, plan 032 J4, plan 029), answering f1d37d2e. Order unchanged: 121a8913, then 7c0e8181, then J4.\n\n1. The S0 prerequisite is disposed. MVP S0 (the deployment and host probe, notes/2026-10-16-repo-in-ai-mvp-plan.md section \"S0\") was never filed and has no finding. J4 does not wait for it. The hold-staging probe that S0 would have made becomes J4's first witness step: stage one hold on the chosen provider from a scratch room on the rehearsal deployment before the fork path is built, and record the observed run in the J4 note. When S0 is filed, it reads that result instead of repeating it. Plan 032 draft 3 records this.\n\n2. The rule extension. OPERATION_RULES in packages/derive/src/capability/hold.ts has rules for stage, check, mint, revoke, delete and deletion, and none for the operations `fork` and `head` that the opening derives, so a fork today stays `creating` whatever the host answers. J4 adds the two missing outcome rules, and nothing else:\n   - `head`: a confirmed read gives the seed commit and opens the `fork` operation; refused or unknown follows the attempt pattern of `stage`.\n   - `fork`: confirmed makes the fork `created` with its id and name; refused opens the next attempt up to HOLD_ATTEMPTS.fork and then `failed`; unknown stays `creating`, and the next attempt uses a new name, as docs/hosts.md records for a lost creation answer.\n   Selection, mint, revoke and the explicit `retire` step stay as they are; the chosen fork publishes through `selected`. Automatic end and sweeping of a hold's fork (plan 029's lifecycle) is later work, not J4; the explicit retire is the J4 path.\n   Version: hold@1 keeps its name if the head shows two things in its note: the judge today records nothing or refuses an outcome of a `fork` or `head` operation, and no deployed room journal holds such an outcome entry (one census read of the three Workers). Then the addition derives records only for entries that never existed, and every recorded meaning is preserved. If either fails, the rules go in hold@2 with hold@1 unchanged. Either way the head carries a kernel-gate section under docs/kernel.md section 7, and the checker reviews it as such.\n\n3. Provider scope: Artifacts first, bounded. J4's adapter creates the fork in the destination's own Artifacts namespace (plan 029), mints the scoped write token for the hold's agent and the read token for the room, revokes on hold end, and publishes the selected fork. Authenticated lane lineage and hold-bound private custody are in scope because the acceptance needs them. GitHub is a separate child, filed after J4 lands, unless the Artifacts path shows the provider interface must change. The older plan's expiry-only statement on GitHub does not govern.\n\nThe acceptance stands as filed: two agents push to their own hold's forks on the rehearsal deployment, the old token fails at the provider after its hold ends, and the change publishes from the chosen fork. The planner deploys when J4 is reviewed.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}